# Laravel Backend Conventions

## Layered Pattern

`Controller (thin) → Service (business logic) → Repository (optional) → Eloquent Model`

- Controllers only orchestrate: validate via `FormRequest`, delegate to a service, return a `JsonResource`.
- Services contain all business rules; inject via constructor.
- Models stay clean: relationships, scopes, casts, accessors only — no business decisions.

## Request / Response

- Input validation: `app/Http/Requests/*Request.php` extending `FormRequest`.
- Output shape: `app/Http/Resources/*Resource.php` / `*Collection.php`.
- Use Laravel's pagination helpers (`->paginate()`, `->cursorPaginate()`); never hand-roll pagination arrays.

## Routes

- All API routes in `routes/api.php` under `/api/v1/` prefix.
- Group by domain (auth, catalog, cart, order, ai, admin-stats).
- Apply middleware: `auth:sanctum`, `throttle:api`, custom policies.

## Enums

Use enums in `app/Enums/` instead of magic strings (existing: `BookLanguage`, `ReviewStatus`). Register via `$casts` on the model.

## Authorization

Use `Policy` + `Gate` — never hardcode role checks inside controllers. Register policies in `AuthServiceProvider`.

## Database Reference

Before writing new queries, migrations, or model relationships, read [backend/docs/database_schema.md](backend/docs/database_schema.md) to verify table names, columns, FKs, and indexes. Avoid duplicate migrations or column typos.
